d moon knight and  kazaat with marvel's flagship titles for  that push comic book fans still argue  whether the move to the direct market  was a good one but for mench and  cincovitch it meant more royalties  because they didn't need to sell as many  copies for the comic to turn a profit it  also meant more work since the comics  were printed with only in-house ads and  the creative team had to turn in 25  pages of story every issue instead of  19.  artist bill sinkovic whose unique style  is as recognizable as it can be jarring  began his comic book career drawing moon  nights tsinkovic was a second year art  student when he brought a portfolio to  the offices of dc comics but it  unknowingly picked precisely the wrong  time to try and join the dc team the  comics company was going through rough  times and was about to cut loose many of  the artists it already had still  syncovich's talent was evidence so  batman artist neil adams whose art  syncovich readily admits he based his  early work on called jim shooter at  marvel comics and told the controversial  editor-in-chief he had a new artist for  him both cinco vich and mensch guessed  it was at least in part the comparison  to adams and to the enduring industry  opinion that moon knight was marvel's  batman that paired cinco vich and mensch  regardless zinkovic proved his talent  and moonlight readers watched the  artist's work evolve into something  closer to the distinct style that made  the artist such an integral figure in  franchises like daredevil new mutants  and legion  according to mench cinkovic had trouble  meeting deadlines on moon night editor  dennis o'neil's solution was to tell  mench to write a seven-page backup story  that o'neill would give to another  artist then that backup would be ready  for some month when cincovich absolutely  needed it to meet the deadline according  to mench once he wrote the backup called  hit it o'neal screwed up instead of  sending the backup to a different artist  he sent it to shinkovich zinkovic told  mench hit it was the best thing he'd  written and the artist was convinced  that using larger panels and other  methods he could stretch it into a full  length story he succeeded and submitted  hit it as the main story for moon knight  issue 26. unfortunately he turned in the  pages so late that o'neal called mention  to the marvel officers from his home in  pennsylvania to script the pages at a  closet sized room with a typewriter hit  it was about a man randomly attacking  every person he meets and readers  eventually learn the criminal's violence  stems from severe childhood abuse  zinkovich suffered his own trauma from  childhood which at least in part  explained his drive to turn what was  supposed to be a seven-page story into  something else moon knight issue 26  marked the emotional end of the series  for cincovich though he stayed on for  four more issues and drew the covers for  the remainder of the series  before our moonlight series was  announced as part of phase 4 of the  marvel cinematic universe there have  been noise about an adaptation for years  the name mark specter was mentioned on  an episode of the short-lived blade the  series then marvel studios partnered  with no equal entertainment to develop a  show based on the hero the series never  came to fruition however nor did  long-running rumors claiming moon knight  would be added to the list of critically  acclaimed marvel netflix shows i'm not  seeking penance for what i've done  father  i'm asking forgiveness  for what i'm about to do  similarly key players of the marvel  cinematic universe and netflix marvel  shows toyed with the idea of getting a  moon knight adaptation made one such  person is guardians of the galaxy  director james gunn he tweeted in  january 2017 that while his workload  prevented him from making a moonlight  film he floated a premise for it past  marvel studios additionally netflix  daredevil showrunner stephen s denite  told ign i